\cf0 \strokec2 The one-sentence version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0 \cf0 \strokec2 RC2 places fake safes like a chess grandmaster who simultaneously sees every thief route, rotates the pieces so thieves can never learn the pattern, maximises credit by recognising that the vault room catches all three thieves at once, and can hand you a signed certificate proving no better placement exists \'97 while every other solver is just guessing\
\

\f2\b The three equations that contain the whole paper:
\f3\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 FM_effective (Eq.18)  \'d7  Q_k(x) (Eq.9)  
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f3   r*(x) = min_\uc0\u920  Q_k (Eq.16)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 FM_effective explains why one trap is worth 1.63\'d7 more than greedy thinks. Q_k(x) adds up all the credit from all the traps. r* takes the worst case across all four attacker types. RC2 maximises r*. That is the dissertation.\
