\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 ==== Level 1 \'97 Understand what problem is actually being solved\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Before touching any math, you need to internalize the core question:\

\f2\b "Where do I put fake computer services, for how long, and in what pattern, so that no matter which type of attacker shows up, I catch as many of them as possible before they reach the real systems \'97 and I can prove mathematically that my placement is the best possible?"
\f3\b0 \
Everything in the paper is just a precise formulation of that one question. If you can explain it in plain English to a non-technical person using the bank robbery example, you are ready for Level 2.\

\f2\b Practice this:
\f3\b0  Explain the force-multiplier to someone who has never heard of MaxSAT. If they understand why one fake safe catches three robbers, you have the intuition.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
