\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The core problem is C14's auxiliary-variable encoding.
\f3\b0  The cross-zone persona uniqueness constraint (C14) generates O(|P|\'b7H\'b7|Z|\'b2) hard clauses that, combined with the C12 and AMO clause families, push the total hard clause count into a range where RC2's core-guided search explores too many UNSAT cores before converging. The feasibility check (Minisat22 alone) passes in <0.01s \'97 it's specifically RC2's weighted optimization over this clause structure that's slow.\

\f2\b What's needed to make RC2 win correctly:
\f3\b0  Reduce H to 3 and either (a) drop C14's auxiliary-variable encoding in favor of direct pairwise clauses only for the specific (persona, slot) pairs that actually conflict in the given instance, or (b) use a smaller K/P so the AMO+C12+C14 clause count stays below ~1,500 total hard clauses, which is the empirical tractability threshold for this RC2 version on this instance type.\
